THOUGHT: NullAway complains that the copy constructor may not initialize the non-null field `region` on all paths, likely because `drawable` could be null or `drawable.region` might be considered nullable. A safe fix is to defensively handle a null `drawable` and ensure `region` is always assigned a non-null value, e.g., by delegating to the no-arg constructor and then conditionally copying the region. I’ll modify the constructor accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count decreases by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '48,51c\  public TextureRegionDrawable(TextureRegionDrawable drawable) {
    this();
    if (drawable != null && drawable.region != null) {
      setRegion(drawable.region);
    }
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/utils/TextureRegionDrawable.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error(s)\]" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

